WEBVTT

00:00:07.966 --> 00:00:09.509
( wind whistling )

00:00:09.593 --> 00:00:13.138
Such a good boy, really.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.973
Oh, such a...

00:00:15.807 --> 00:00:18.184
CHARLIE:
Grandpa?

00:00:18.226 --> 00:00:19.394
( gasps )

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:21.187
( quietly ):
You fell asleep.

00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:22.355
Have you got it?

00:00:25.942 --> 00:00:29.696
Which end should we open first?

00:00:29.779 --> 00:00:32.115
Just do it quick,
like a Band-Aid.

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:39.748
( foil crinkles, grunts )

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:51.801
( wind whistling )

00:00:54.929 --> 00:00:57.891
( inhales deeply )

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:04.439
Did you see that
some kid in Russia

00:01:04.522 --> 00:01:05.982
found the last
golden ticket?

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.401
Yes, it was in the paper
this morning.

00:01:08.443 --> 00:01:09.736
Good boy.

00:01:09.778 --> 00:01:12.238
Come on, George.
Good boy.

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:22.749
( wind whistling )

00:01:30.965 --> 00:01:33.218
( wind whistling )

00:01:42.811 --> 00:01:45.063
♪ ♪

00:01:47.732 --> 00:01:50.443
( gasps )

00:01:56.366 --> 00:01:58.451
( bell jingles )

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:04.916
One Wonka Whipple-Scrumptious

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:06.626
Fudgemallow
Delight, please.

00:02:06.710 --> 00:02:08.044
Okay.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.921
Yep.

00:02:12.132 --> 00:02:13.383
( cash register opens )

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.136
The nerve of some people.

00:02:16.177 --> 00:02:18.555
( chuckles ):
I know.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:21.182
Forging a ticket.
Come on.

00:02:21.266 --> 00:02:23.935
( chuckles )

00:02:29.691 --> 00:02:32.736
( gasps )

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.071
It’s a golden ticket.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:38.700
You found Wonka’s

00:02:38.783 --> 00:02:40.493
last golden ticket!

00:02:41.494 --> 00:02:43.455
In my shop, too!

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.999
Listen, I’ll buy
it from you.

00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:47.500
I’ll give you $50.

00:02:47.584 --> 00:02:48.585
And a new bicycle.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:50.044
Are you crazy?

00:02:50.128 --> 00:02:51.129
I’d give him $500
for that ticket.

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.922
You want to sell me
your ticket

00:02:53.006 --> 00:02:54.424
for $500, young man?

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.176
That’s enough of that!
Leave the kid alone!

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:59.929
Listen,
don’t let anyone have it.

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:01.848
Take it straight home,

00:03:01.890 --> 00:03:02.807
you understand?

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:05.143
Thank you.

00:03:11.483 --> 00:03:14.778
Mom! Dad!

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:17.030
I found it!

00:03:17.113 --> 00:03:19.407
The last golden ticket--

00:03:19.491 --> 00:03:20.992
it’s mine!

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:32.796
♪ ♪

00:03:34.631 --> 00:03:36.466
Yippee!

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.802
( humming happily )

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:42.597
( humming continues )

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.932
Here.

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:45.975
Read this aloud.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.561
Let’s hear exactly
what it says.

00:03:48.603 --> 00:03:49.896
"Greetings to you

00:03:49.979 --> 00:03:52.357
"the lucky finder of
this golden ticket

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:54.234
"from Mr. Willy Wonka.

00:03:54.275 --> 00:03:55.985
"I shake you warmly
by the hand.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.654
"For now I do invite you

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.155
"to come to my factory

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.574
and be my guest
for one whole day."

00:04:01.616 --> 00:04:03.076
VIOLET:
"I, Willy Wonka,

00:04:03.159 --> 00:04:05.453
"will conduct you
around the factory myself,

00:04:05.537 --> 00:04:07.914
showing you everything
there is to see."

00:04:07.997 --> 00:04:09.624
"Afterwards,
when it is time to leave,

00:04:09.707 --> 00:04:12.669
"you will be escorted home by
a procession of large trucks,

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:16.756
each one filled with all the
chocolate you could ever eat."

00:04:16.840 --> 00:04:18.258
VERUCA:
"And remember,

00:04:18.299 --> 00:04:20.218
"one of you lucky five children

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:24.097
"will receive an extra prize
beyond your wildest imagination.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:26.808
Now, here are
your instructions:"

00:04:26.891 --> 00:04:28.268
"On the first of February,

00:04:28.351 --> 00:04:30.436
"you must come to the factory
gates at 10:00 a.m. sharp.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.730
"You’re allowed to bring
one member of your family

00:04:32.772 --> 00:04:34.065
"to look after you.

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:36.943
Till then, Willy Wonka."

00:04:36.985 --> 00:04:38.945
MRS. BUCKET:
First of February.

00:04:39.028 --> 00:04:40.947
But that’s tomorrow.

00:04:40.989 --> 00:04:42.949
Then there’s not a moment
to lose, Charlie.

00:04:43.032 --> 00:04:44.325
Wash your face,
comb your hair,

00:04:44.409 --> 00:04:45.285
scrub your hands,

00:04:45.326 --> 00:04:46.911
brush your teeth,
blow your nose...

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.371
And get that mud
off your pants.

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:49.956
MRS. BUCKET:
Now we must all try
and keep very calm.

00:04:50.039 --> 00:04:52.292
First thing that we
have to decide is this:

00:04:52.333 --> 00:04:55.628
Who is going with Charlie
to the factory?

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:56.588
I will.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:57.630
I’ll take him.

00:04:57.672 --> 00:04:58.798
You leave it to me.

00:04:58.882 --> 00:04:59.966
How about you, dear?

00:05:00.008 --> 00:05:01.050
Don’t you think
you ought to go?

00:05:01.134 --> 00:05:04.846
Well... Grandpa Joe
seems to know

00:05:04.929 --> 00:05:06.556
more about it
than we do.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.601
Provided, of course,
he feels well enough.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.935
Yippee!

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:12.478
( chuckling )

00:05:12.562 --> 00:05:13.688
No.

00:05:13.771 --> 00:05:15.899
We’re not going.

00:05:18.192 --> 00:05:20.987
A woman offered me $500
for the ticket.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.281
I bet someone else
would pay more.

00:05:23.323 --> 00:05:27.201
We need the money more
than we need the chocolate.

00:05:31.956 --> 00:05:34.417
( bed springs creak )

00:05:36.461 --> 00:05:37.795
Young man,

00:05:37.837 --> 00:05:39.547
come here.

00:05:42.508 --> 00:05:45.803
There’s plenty of money
out there.

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:48.139
They print more
every day.

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:51.559
But this ticket--

00:05:51.643 --> 00:05:54.687
there’s only five of them
in the whole world,

00:05:54.771 --> 00:05:57.857
and that’s all there’s ever
going to be.

00:05:57.899 --> 00:05:59.943
Only a dummy
would give this up

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:03.696
for something
as common as money.

00:06:03.738 --> 00:06:06.532
Are you a dummy?

00:06:06.616 --> 00:06:08.493
No, sir.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:11.037
Then get that mud
off your pants.

00:06:11.079 --> 00:06:13.456
You’ve got a factory
to go to.

